  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Deloitte Consulting obligated $2.2B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date, across 547 awards with an average award size of $3.9M. Obligations fell 27.3% year over year. Obligations peaked at $3.3B in FY24 and then declined to $3B in FY25 and $2.2B in FY26. The General Services Administration is the largest buyer in FY2026 to date, with $652M in obligations, followed by the Department of Defense with $317M and the Department of Veterans Affairs with $311M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market by NAICS, with $1.1B in obligations, followed by Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services with $467M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences with $248M. Other notable FY2026 to date markets include Engineering Services at $202M and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $60M. Current-year totals are partial, and the largest-agency and market concentrations show Deloitte Consulting still centered on IT systems and management consulting work for civilian and defense customers.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have Deloitte Consulting obligations trended recently?",
        "body": "Deloitte Consulting obligations rose from $2.4B in FY21 to $3.3B in FY24 and then declined to $3B in FY25 and $2.2B in FY26. Obligations fell 27.3% year over year for FY2026 to date. Current-year totals are partial and FY26 is reported as year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers and what services dominate?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration is the largest buyer in FY2026 to date at $652M, followed by the Department of Defense at $317M and the Department of Veterans Affairs at $311M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market at $1.1B, followed by Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $467M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $248M."
      }
    ]
  },
